# Common — language-agnostic baseline, plus the Python/Qt entries
# added at P01 (LWSM-1002).
#
# This repository is destined to be PUBLIC, so everything here is
# also a privacy control: a file ignored late is a file already in
# the history, and history is public forever. Anything holding
# machine paths, personal data or another project's internals
# belongs in this list BEFORE the first push (LWSM-1045).

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
\#*\#

# Secrets / local env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code (local settings, history, allowlist — mostly personal).
# Drop the trailing slash so the negations below can re-include
# specific files; with `.claude/` git short-circuits at the
# directory and ignores the !.claude/foo lines.
.claude/*
# Team-shared Claude Code config that SHOULD be in version control:
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/workflow.md

# Logs / runtime
*.log
*.pid
*.sock

# Coverage / sanitizers
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
coverage.*
.coverage
lcov.info

# Core dumps
core
core.*
*.core
vgcore.*

# Scratch
scratch/
tmp/
Screenshot_*.png
screenshot*.png

# Python (LWSM-1002)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
# uv.lock is COMMITTED, not ignored — it is what makes `uv sync --locked` in
# scripts/local-ci.sh reproduce the same versions locally and in CI. An
# ignored lockfile means the two runs can resolve differently, which is the
# exact drift the shared script exists to prevent. `--locked`, NOT `--frozen`:
# --frozen exits 0 against a lock that disagrees with pyproject.toml
# (dependencies.md § 2.5).

# Qt / PySide6
*.qmlc
*.jsc
qrc_*.py
ui_*.py
*.pro.user

# AppImage build output (LWSM-1021)
*.AppImage
AppDir/
appimagetool*

# Runtime state this app writes. Never in the repo, and named here so a
# developer running the app from the source tree cannot commit their own
# project list — which would publish their machine's directory layout.
/projects.json
/settings.json
/app.log*
/logs/

# Roadmap ID counter — derived per-machine cache, not source.
# True high-water mark is the highest ID across ROADMAP.md +
# CHANGELOG.md + docs/roadmap/*.md (roadmap-format.md § 3.5.1).
.roadmap-counter

# Author-private working notes (LWSM-1045). This repository is public;
# docs/private/ holds the concrete project inventory and the per-project
# adoption prompt, which name real services, ports and paths on the
# author's machine. The public docs refer to them by neutral label.
docs/private/

# Audit scan output. Generated, one more pair of files every run, and it embeds
# absolute paths from the machine that ran it — this is a public repo. The
# durable record of what a scan found lives in ROADMAP.md and
# docs/audit-allowlist.md, which are written for a reader.
#
# The gitleaks config below it is an INPUT, not output: it carries the
# allowlist that makes a run reproducible, so it stays tracked.
.audit_cache/*
!.audit_cache/.gitleaks-audit-run.toml
